Test fixtures: small images that tests/test_cd.c and tests/test_dmg.c read,
made by tools Blue doesn't have (it only reads these formats). Each was made
from an input Blue's tests make again themselves, so the tests compare what
Blue reads from a fixture with that input, byte for byte (or, for the lossy
audio, by its length and how close it is).

Inputs (made by a program linked with Blue's own hfs.c, as the tests make them):

- vol.img: a 400K HFS volume, hfs_format(..., 409600, "Packed", 0xB0000000,
  { "Read Me", 'TEXT', 'ttxt', "Hello from a compressed image" }).
- Game.cue / game.bin: test_single_bin()'s disc in tests/test_cd.c (an HFS
  volume of 400 2048-byte sectors, "Test CD", as raw mode 1 sectors; 150
  sectors of silence; audio track 2, 100 sectors of pattern 2; audio track 3,
  50 sectors of pattern 3), its last sector whole; Data.cue, the data track
  alone (data.bin, its first 400 sectors).
- tone.raw: 30 sectors of 16-bit stereo, 440 Hz left, 660 Hz right, at 8000.

Made with:

- packed-zlib.dmg, packed-bzip2.dmg, packed-lzfse.dmg, packed-lzma.dmg,
  packed-adc.dmg: `hdiutil convert vol.img -format UDZO` (UDBZ, ULFO, ULMO,
  UDCO) on macOS 27.2 (Apple's own UDIF writer: zlib, bzip2, LZFSE, xz and ADC
  chunks).
- game.chd: `chdman createcd -i Game.cue -o game.chd` (cdlz, cdzl, cdfl);
  game-cdzs.chd: the same with `-c cdzs,cdfl` (zstd); data-cdzl.chd:
  `chdman createcd -c cdzl -i Data.cue`. chdman 0.289, built from MAME's
  source (src/tools/chdman.cpp).
- tone.flac, tone.mp3 (`-c:a libmp3lame -b:a 160k`), tone.ogg (ffmpeg's own
  Vorbis encoder, `-c:a vorbis -strict -2 -q:a 4`), tone-mono.flac (the left
  channel alone, `-af pan=mono|c0=c0`), tone-22k.mp3 (0.1 s at 22050 Hz, to be
  refused): `ffmpeg -f s16le -ar 44100 -ac 2 -i tone.raw ...`, FFmpeg 9.0.2.

